<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngamiland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngamiland is the region of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ngami">Lake Ngami</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okavango-delta">Okavango Delta</a>, named after the lake. It was the territory of the Batawana chiefdom and was brought into the Bechuanaland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> in the late 19th century. It now forms most of Botswana's North-West District, with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maun">Maun</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ngamiland.jpg" alt="Ngamiland" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: jonrawlinson · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maun_Botswana2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
